            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Perform the water drop test. Drip a tablespoon of water onto the most heavily used area of the marble (usually near the sink) and wait 15 minutes. If the water beads up into a tight sphere like rain on a freshly waxed car, your sealer is intact. If the water flattens out and the marble underneath turns dark, the stone is absorbing the moisture and must be resealed immediately. Note: Check several areas, as sealer wears out faster on \"work zones\" compared to decorative corners.",
          },
        },
