          "@type": "Question",
          name: "My countertop is already stained. Can I seal over it?",
          acceptedAnswer: {
            "@type": "Answer",
            text: "Never seal over an active stain. The sealer will lock the stain inside the pores permanently, making removal virtually impossible. Treat existing stains using a specialized poultice powder mixed with hydrogen peroxide or a commercial stain remover designed for marble. The poultice draws the stain out over 24-48 hours. Once the stone is clear and dry, then apply the sealer. For oily stains, a \"solvent poultice\" using acetone and baking soda is often required to break down the surface tension of the grease.",
          },
        },
